        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Lint: HTML tables should have explicit <tbody> tag]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41774</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41774"/>
        <updated>2025-11-02T04:28:41.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">HTML <code class="notranslate">&lt;tbody&gt;</code> elements can have both start/end tags omitted, but it's still present in the DOM, which can be extremely unintuitive for selectors/DOM operations. Instead of relying on this implicit behavior, it's better to make the <code class="notranslate">&lt;tbody&gt;</code> explicit where possible.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR should be very easy to review with hide whitespace turned on.</p>]]></content>
